# Directory spec for the shipped `vynil` system package box.

Spec: box/vynil

Platform: Vynil package/Handlebars/Rhai

Purpose:
  The Vynil self-hosting package: a `system` package that installs and configures the Vynil
  controller, its diagnostic server, RBAC, priority classes, and certificates into a cluster,
  and is published as an OCI image consumed through a `@JukeBox` source.

Structure:
  ./package.yaml: Package manifest — name, type `system`, category `core`, images, resources,
    requirements, recommendations, and options
  ./systems/*.yaml.hbs: Rendered Kubernetes manifests (controller, service, rbac, diagnostics,
    certificates, priority classes)
  ./crds/crd.yaml: CRD bundle shipped by this package, generated from the Rust CRD types
  ./tests/: Vynil package test manifests run by `agent package test`

Owns:
  ./package.yaml
  ./systems/**
  ./crds/crd.yaml
  ./tests/**

Must:
  Keep the `app_version` and the three `images` tags consistent with the workspace version in
    /Cargo.toml and the published agent, operator, and server images.
  Declare the monitoring and cert-manager CRD recommendations, since the diagnostics depend on
    them.
  Generate ./crds/crd.yaml from the Rust CRD types through `cargo cmd generate_crd`, never by hand.
  Render every manifest with the Vynil Handlebars context helpers, using `instance.appslug` for
    resource naming.

Must not:
  Hand-edit ./crds/crd.yaml, or let it drift from the Rust types that generate it.
  Grant cluster-admin to the diagnostic server beyond what tenant-scoped read access requires.

Depends on:
  /agent/Dockerfile.sdd
  /operator/Dockerfile.sdd
  /server/Dockerfile.sdd

Done when:
  `agent package build` produces an installable image, `agent package test ./box/vynil` is green,
    and the CRD bundle matches the Rust types.

Tasks:
  [ ] #0 Confirm ./tests/ manifests cover install, upgrade, and uninstall for the core and
    monitoring variants.
